reagent-name-bz = bz
reagent-desc-bz = A powerful hallucinogen that also puts slimepeople to sleep.

reagent-name-healium = healium
reagent-desc-healium = A potent sleeping agent with regenerative properties.

reagent-name-nitrium = nitrium
reagent-desc-nitrium = A powerful stimulant; when inhaled, increases speed and stamina.

reagent-name-pluoxium = pluoxium
reagent-desc-pluoxium = A gas that saturates blood with a large amount of oxygen without being an oxidizer.

reagent-name-hyper-nob = hyper-noblium
reagent-desc-hyper-nob = The noblest gas of all. Large amounts of hyper-noblium actively prevent reactions from occurring.

reagent-name-proto-nitrate = proto-nitrate
reagent-desc-proto-nitrate = An unstable gas that reacts differently with various gases.

reagent-name-zauker = zauker
reagent-desc-zauker = An extremely toxic gas; its production is strictly regulated, in addition to its difficulty of manufacture. Rapidly breaks down upon contact with nitrogen.

reagent-name-halon = halon
reagent-desc-halon = A powerful fire suppressant. At high temperatures, it absorbs oxygen and cools the room.

reagent-name-helium = helium
reagent-desc-helium = An inert gas obtained from the synthesis of hydrogen and its derivatives.

reagent-name-anti-nob = anti-noblium
reagent-desc-anti-nob = We still don't know what it does, but it's expensive.

reagent-name-electrovae = electrovae
reagent-desc-electrovae = An ominously humming gas.

reagent-name-charged-electrovae = charged electrovae
reagent-desc-charged-electrovae = An electrically charged gas. It tingles the skin.

